WEBVTT

00:00:33.034 --> 00:00:34.285
This is awesome!

00:00:34.369 --> 00:00:35.870
I've been waiting a 1000 years

00:00:35.954 --> 00:00:37.622
to see a Beastie Boys show.

00:00:37.705 --> 00:00:39.082
Can I get anybody a beer?

00:00:39.165 --> 00:00:40.250
Sure.

00:00:44.754 --> 00:00:45.755
Ah...

00:00:45.839 --> 00:00:48.299
Ladies and gentlemen,
here to lay down

00:00:48.383 --> 00:00:52.554
some old, old,
incredibly old school beats,

00:00:52.637 --> 00:00:55.557
the Beastie Boys!

00:01:01.271 --> 00:01:04.649
Well, now, don't you tell me to smile

00:01:04.732 --> 00:01:06.860
You stick around
I'll make it worth your while

00:01:06.943 --> 00:01:09.195
Like numbers beyond what you can dial

00:01:09.279 --> 00:01:11.531
Maybe it's because we're so versatile

00:01:11.614 --> 00:01:13.658
"Style, profile," I said

00:01:13.741 --> 00:01:15.994
It always brings me back
When I hear, "Ooh, child"

00:01:16.077 --> 00:01:17.078
From the Hudson river...

00:01:17.161 --> 00:01:18.162
impressive.

00:01:18.246 --> 00:01:21.332
They're busting mad rhymes
with an 80% success rate.

00:01:21.416 --> 00:01:23.793
I believe that qualifies as ill.

00:01:23.877 --> 00:01:25.962
At least from a technical standpoint.

00:01:26.045 --> 00:01:27.255
Will you guys shut up?

00:01:27.338 --> 00:01:28.464
I'm trying to look cool.

00:01:29.966 --> 00:01:31.968
-Tammy D gets biz on the crops
-Crops

00:01:32.051 --> 00:01:34.012
Beastie Boys known to let the beat...

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:36.222
Mm, drop?

00:01:36.306 --> 00:01:38.308
Ow! How's it going?

00:01:38.391 --> 00:01:40.185
Ow! Enjoying the show?

00:01:40.268 --> 00:01:41.269
OOH! OW!

00:01:41.352 --> 00:01:43.563
Don't forget to pick up a t-shirt.

00:01:43.646 --> 00:01:46.399
Wow, an old-fashioned mosh pit.

00:01:46.482 --> 00:01:47.483
Come on, guys.

00:01:47.567 --> 00:01:50.236
Tonight we're going to party
like it's 1999...

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:51.321
again.

00:01:58.745 --> 00:02:00.246
Ow! Hey, watch it!

00:02:06.294 --> 00:02:08.713
Man, these guys rock harder than ever.

00:02:08.796 --> 00:02:10.924
Oh, my

00:02:11.007 --> 00:02:12.675
It's a mirage

00:02:12.759 --> 00:02:14.719
Telling you all it's a...

00:02:14.802 --> 00:02:18.932
Sabotage

00:02:19.015 --> 00:02:21.726
Sabotage, yeah

00:02:21.809 --> 00:02:23.019
Peace! We out!

00:02:31.152 --> 00:02:32.237
Hey, Bender.

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:33.613
Hey, Fender.

00:02:33.696 --> 00:02:36.115
Man, I haven't seen you since high school.

00:02:36.199 --> 00:02:37.992
You still working at Jack in The Box?

00:02:38.076 --> 00:02:39.244
Not anymore, baby.

00:02:39.327 --> 00:02:40.703
I'm with the band.

00:02:42.956 --> 00:02:45.083
Oh-oh, yeah.

00:02:45.166 --> 00:02:46.417
Hey, fellas, hey.

00:02:46.501 --> 00:02:49.212
I want you to meet my friends,
Bender, Fry, and Leela.

00:02:49.295 --> 00:02:52.340
You know, we're really not that
interested in meeting them.

00:02:52.423 --> 00:02:54.634
Wow, I love you guys.

00:02:54.717 --> 00:02:55.885
Back in the 20th century,

00:02:55.969 --> 00:02:57.554
I had all five of your albums.

00:02:57.637 --> 00:03:00.306
That was a 1000 years ago.
Now we got seven.

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:02.684
Cool. Can I borrow the new ones?

00:03:02.767 --> 00:03:03.977
And a couple of blank tapes?

00:03:05.478 --> 00:03:07.939
Hey, Bender,
why don't we ditch these organ sacks

00:03:08.022 --> 00:03:09.274
and hit the real party?

00:03:09.357 --> 00:03:12.193
Count me in.
I'm going to drink till I reboot.

00:03:19.242 --> 00:03:21.494
Hey, what kind of party is this?

00:03:21.578 --> 00:03:23.746
There's no booze and only one hooker.

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:25.456
Don't be a drag, man.

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:26.958
We're jacking on.

00:03:29.919 --> 00:03:33.006
O-o-o-h, y-y-yeah!

00:03:33.089 --> 00:03:34.132
Want a jolt?

00:03:34.215 --> 00:03:36.009
Uh, hey, I'm no square,

00:03:36.092 --> 00:03:37.552
but isn't that counter-indicated

00:03:37.635 --> 00:03:38.970
by my operations manual?

00:03:42.599 --> 00:03:44.267
Come on, Bender. Grab a jack.

00:03:44.350 --> 00:03:45.810
I told these guys you were cool.

00:03:46.311 --> 00:03:50.190
Well, if jacking on will make
strangers think I'm cool,

00:03:50.273 --> 00:03:51.482
I'll do it.

00:03:53.484 --> 00:03:55.695
Whoa!

00:04:07.749 --> 00:04:08.958
Mmm!

00:04:24.015 --> 00:04:26.601
Easy, baby, you don't want
to get hooked on this stuff.

00:04:26.684 --> 00:04:30.563
Ah, no need to worry.
I don't have an addictive personality.

00:04:38.446 --> 00:04:41.491
Hey, uh, Bender, what are we doing
in this bad neighborhood?

00:04:41.574 --> 00:04:43.243
Shut up, Square!

00:04:46.454 --> 00:04:48.039
I'll just be a minute.

00:05:01.761 --> 00:05:03.054
Wretched sinner unit.

00:05:03.137 --> 00:05:05.765
The path to robot heaven lies here,

00:05:05.849 --> 00:05:07.976
in the good book 3.0.

00:05:08.059 --> 00:05:09.769
Hey, do I preach to you

00:05:09.853 --> 00:05:12.647
when you're lying stoned in the gutter?

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:14.107
No.

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:15.275
So beat it!

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:17.235
Tsk-tsk-tsk.

00:05:19.112 --> 00:05:20.321
Who was that guy?

00:05:20.405 --> 00:05:21.406
Your mama.

00:05:21.489 --> 00:05:23.408
Now shut up and drag me to work.

00:05:29.622 --> 00:05:31.332
Our electric bill is climbing faster

00:05:31.416 --> 00:05:32.917
than a green snake up a sugarcane.

00:05:33.001 --> 00:05:34.919
Obviously, someone 'round here

00:05:35.003 --> 00:05:37.088
been wasting a whole heap of juice.

00:05:37.172 --> 00:05:39.174
- Probably you.
- Me?

00:05:41.009 --> 00:05:42.177
Good morning, Bender.

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:44.888
None of your business! Get off my back!

00:05:46.556 --> 00:05:47.640
What's his problem?

00:05:47.724 --> 00:05:48.808
if I didn't know better,

00:05:48.892 --> 00:05:51.311
I'd almost think
he was abusing electricity.

00:05:51.394 --> 00:05:52.645
Bender? No way.

00:05:54.272 --> 00:05:56.232
I definitely would have noticed something.

00:05:58.443 --> 00:06:01.738
Bender, why are you spending
so much time in the bathroom?

00:06:01.821 --> 00:06:03.531
Are you jacking on in there?

00:06:03.615 --> 00:06:04.949
No! Don't come in!

00:06:05.366 --> 00:06:07.076
Good news, everyone.

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:09.704
Today you'll be delivering
a crate of subpoenas

00:06:09.787 --> 00:06:12.498
to Sicily 8, the mob planet.

00:06:13.708 --> 00:06:16.085
All right, let's get to work!

00:06:16.169 --> 00:06:17.587
I'll be out in a second.

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:28.515
I know Big Vinnie said
he was giving me the kiss of death,

00:06:28.598 --> 00:06:30.683
but I still think he was gay.

00:06:30.767 --> 00:06:32.268
Did he use his tongue?

00:06:32.352 --> 00:06:33.436
A little.

00:06:36.147 --> 00:06:39.651
- Are you okay, Bender?
- None of your business! Get off my back!

00:06:39.734 --> 00:06:42.111
Uh-oh. There seems to be
an electrical disturbance

00:06:42.195 --> 00:06:43.321
in the Coalsack Nebula.

00:06:43.404 --> 00:06:46.366
- A what kind of a disturbance?
- Electrical.

00:06:46.449 --> 00:06:49.536
Anyway, it's going to take
some careful piloting to avoid it.

00:07:06.803 --> 00:07:07.929
We're out of control!

00:07:08.012 --> 00:07:09.806
We're heading straight
into the electric field.

00:07:09.889 --> 00:07:11.975
What's happening? I feel weird.

00:07:15.311 --> 00:07:16.855
Come on, Universe,

00:07:16.938 --> 00:07:19.274
you big, mostly empty wuss!

00:07:19.357 --> 00:07:22.026
Give me all the juice you got!

00:07:29.325 --> 00:07:31.244
Oh, Mama.

00:07:47.677 --> 00:07:48.887
WHAT?

00:07:49.429 --> 00:07:50.930
Bender, we didn't mind

00:07:51.014 --> 00:07:52.849
your drinking or your kleptomania

00:07:52.932 --> 00:07:54.434
or your pornography ring.

00:07:54.517 --> 00:07:56.686
in fact, that's why we loved you.

00:07:56.769 --> 00:07:59.063
But this electricity abuse
crossed the line.

00:07:59.147 --> 00:08:00.565
You almost killed us.

00:08:00.648 --> 00:08:02.901
And you made me feel
like a jerk for trusting you.

00:08:03.359 --> 00:08:06.279
Just like when my friend Richie swore
he wasn't taking drugs

00:08:06.362 --> 00:08:08.364
And then he sold me my mom's VCR.

00:08:08.448 --> 00:08:10.783
And then later, I found out
he was taking drugs.

00:08:10.867 --> 00:08:13.578
You make me ashamed to be your friend.

00:08:13.995 --> 00:08:18.416
Oh, you're right. I'm a lost cause.

00:08:33.306 --> 00:08:35.225
Maybe there's another way.

00:08:38.603 --> 00:08:41.564
Oh, yeah, that's the good stuff.

00:08:44.484 --> 00:08:46.236
What am I doing?

00:08:46.319 --> 00:08:48.738
What have I become?

00:08:49.197 --> 00:08:50.281
Huh?

00:08:51.783 --> 00:08:54.911
I see a lot of fancy robots here today

00:08:54.994 --> 00:08:57.372
made of real shiny metal.

00:08:57.455 --> 00:08:59.958
But that don't impress
the Robot Devil, no, sir.

00:09:00.041 --> 00:09:02.126
- No, sir!
- 'Cause if you're a sinner,

00:09:02.210 --> 00:09:05.463
He's going to plug
his infernal modem in the wall,

00:09:05.547 --> 00:09:09.509
belching smoke and flame,
and he's going to download you

00:09:09.592 --> 00:09:11.219
straight to robot hell.

00:09:11.302 --> 00:09:12.512
Straight to hell!

00:09:12.595 --> 00:09:14.097
So I ask you,

00:09:14.180 --> 00:09:16.891
"Who will stand up and be saved?"

00:09:16.975 --> 00:09:18.810
Who? Who?

00:09:23.356 --> 00:09:24.649
Me.

00:09:31.197 --> 00:09:32.949
And as a further cost-cutting measure,

00:09:33.032 --> 00:09:35.535
I have eliminated the saltwater cooler.

00:09:35.618 --> 00:09:36.995
This is a witch hunt.

00:09:37.078 --> 00:09:40.456
Oh, what a beautiful morning

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:43.710
Oh, what a beautiful day

00:09:43.793 --> 00:09:44.919
Greetings, friends.

00:09:45.003 --> 00:09:46.838
Don't we all look nice today?

00:09:46.921 --> 00:09:49.632
Great. He's whacked out
on electricity again.

00:09:49.716 --> 00:09:51.926
No, I'm whacked out on life.

00:09:52.010 --> 00:09:55.847
My friends, I found religion.

00:09:57.682 --> 00:09:58.892
Religion?

00:09:58.975 --> 00:10:01.603
is this another scam
to get free yarmuikes?

00:10:01.686 --> 00:10:03.229
Give him a break, Fry.

00:10:03.313 --> 00:10:04.981
if this helps Bender clean up his act,

00:10:05.064 --> 00:10:06.858
then I think we should be supportive.

00:10:08.985 --> 00:10:09.986
Wonderful.

00:10:10.069 --> 00:10:12.739
Then you'll all come
to my exceedingly long

00:10:12.822 --> 00:10:15.283
un-air-conditioned baptism ceremony.

00:10:15.575 --> 00:10:18.661
- Um... Oh, i...
- Uh...

00:10:20.288 --> 00:10:23.249
We are gathered here today
to deliver brother Bender

00:10:23.333 --> 00:10:26.377
From the cold, steel grip
of the Robot Devil

00:10:26.461 --> 00:10:30.381
Unto the cold, steel bosom
of our congregation.

00:10:30.590 --> 00:10:31.758
Tell it, Preacher!

00:10:31.841 --> 00:10:33.259
That equals true.

00:10:33.468 --> 00:10:34.761
Brother Bender.

00:10:34.844 --> 00:10:37.555
Do you accept the principles
of Robotology,

00:10:37.639 --> 00:10:40.642
on pain of eternal damnation
in robot hell?

00:10:40.725 --> 00:10:42.477
Yes, I do.

00:10:42.560 --> 00:10:45.021
Then I will now baptize you.

00:10:45.104 --> 00:10:46.856
Press any key to continue.

00:11:02.997 --> 00:11:03.998
Uh, while you're at it

00:11:04.082 --> 00:11:05.792
could you touch up this seam?

00:11:11.256 --> 00:11:12.590
This is unbelievable.

00:11:12.674 --> 00:11:15.301
The old Bender never would
have taken us out to dinner.

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:17.136
The old Bender's gone.

00:11:17.220 --> 00:11:19.347
He won't trouble you anymore.

00:11:19.430 --> 00:11:21.891
Would Monsieur care
to see the wine list?

00:11:25.311 --> 00:11:27.313
No poison for us, thanks.

00:11:27.397 --> 00:11:30.191
I'll stick with good old mineral oil.

00:11:32.193 --> 00:11:34.112
Ah. Functional.

00:11:34.612 --> 00:11:35.989
- Mmm.
- That's mine here.

00:11:36.072 --> 00:11:39.075
Man, I'm hungrier than a green snake
in a sugarcane field.

00:11:39.993 --> 00:11:43.246
Friends, friends,
surely you're not going to eat

00:11:43.329 --> 00:11:45.456
before we say robot grace.

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:47.208
- Oh, man.
- Uh...

00:11:48.793 --> 00:11:50.962
in the name of all that is
good and logical

00:11:51.045 --> 00:11:54.716
we give thanks for the chemical
energy we are about to absorb.

00:11:54.799 --> 00:11:56.718
To quote the prophet Jerematic,

00:11:56.801 --> 00:11:58.136
"One-zero-zero-zero

00:11:58.219 --> 00:12:02.182
"one-zero-one-zero-
one-zero-one-zero-one...

00:12:03.141 --> 00:12:04.934
"zero-zero-one

00:12:05.018 --> 00:12:08.855
"zero-one-one-zero-zero-one...
Two."

00:12:09.105 --> 00:12:10.481
Amen.

00:12:10.565 --> 00:12:12.066
Does that mean we can eat now?

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:13.443
Yes.

00:12:13.735 --> 00:12:18.072
But first, since I love you all so much

00:12:18.323 --> 00:12:20.992
I'd like to give everyone hugs.

00:12:21.075 --> 00:12:22.785
Come here, Fry.

00:12:22.952 --> 00:12:24.454
Oh, uh, but I don't want to.

00:12:29.584 --> 00:12:33.087
Fry, you're my friend.

00:12:35.548 --> 00:12:37.926
Come on, everyone line up for a hug.

00:12:38.009 --> 00:12:41.304
Let's tear down some emotional walls.

00:12:48.853 --> 00:12:50.313
What are you doing to my ship?

00:12:50.396 --> 00:12:52.148
Sanctifying it.

00:12:53.566 --> 00:12:56.528
There. That ought to convert
a few tailgaters.

00:12:57.362 --> 00:13:00.114
Bender's stupid religion
is driving me nuts.

00:13:00.198 --> 00:13:01.324
Amen.

00:13:01.407 --> 00:13:03.910
If only he had joined
a mainstream religion

00:13:03.993 --> 00:13:05.912
like Orpah-ism or voodoo.

00:13:05.995 --> 00:13:07.747
We've got to get the old Bender back.

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:09.541
And I think I know a way to do it.

00:13:09.624 --> 00:13:13.753
We have to reacquaint him
with a little thing called sleaze.

00:13:17.423 --> 00:13:19.342
I can't believe somebody hired

00:13:19.425 --> 00:13:20.718
an interstellar spaceship

00:13:20.802 --> 00:13:23.304
to deliver a package to Atlantic city.

00:13:23.388 --> 00:13:24.889
What are we delivering, anyway?

00:13:24.973 --> 00:13:26.808
Uh... This.

00:13:27.725 --> 00:13:29.227
Where are we delivering it to?

00:13:29.644 --> 00:13:32.063
Uh... Here.

00:13:32.397 --> 00:13:34.399
Another job well done.

00:13:34.691 --> 00:13:36.150
Now back to the office

00:13:36.234 --> 00:13:38.903
for an enjoyable evening
of fasting and repentance.

00:13:39.112 --> 00:13:40.363
Whoa, whoa. Wait, Bender.

00:13:40.446 --> 00:13:44.075
As long as we're here
why don't we take in some exotic dancing?

00:13:44.158 --> 00:13:45.952
Hey, great idea.

00:13:48.997 --> 00:13:51.708
But those girls don't wear cases.

00:13:51.791 --> 00:13:54.085
You can see their bare circuits.

00:13:54.169 --> 00:13:56.004
Come on, it'll be fun.

00:13:56.087 --> 00:13:58.882
Maybe we could even drink
a little fortified wine.

00:13:58.965 --> 00:14:01.593
WhAt? Drinking wine is a sin...

00:14:01.676 --> 00:14:03.970
Even if it is deliciously fortified.

00:14:04.053 --> 00:14:06.139
Hey, Bender, look at that woman's purse.

00:14:06.514 --> 00:14:08.641
It's hanging by a spaghetti strand.

00:14:10.226 --> 00:14:12.645
Thou shalt not snatch.

00:14:12.729 --> 00:14:14.480
And there's Hookerbot 5000.

00:14:14.564 --> 00:14:16.316
She's got a heart of solid gold.

00:14:16.524 --> 00:14:18.359
Hey, Sailing unit.

00:14:18.568 --> 00:14:20.737
Stop tempting me!

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:23.948
For once in my life, I have inner peace.

00:14:24.032 --> 00:14:25.617
That's for losers.

00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:27.452
Come on, sin your heart out.

00:14:27.535 --> 00:14:29.329
- Go nuts.
- Live a little.

00:14:29.412 --> 00:14:31.122
Could you hold my
purse for a minute?

00:14:31.206 --> 00:14:32.373
Go for it, Bender.

00:14:32.457 --> 00:14:33.666
You know you want to.

00:14:34.709 --> 00:14:36.294
Well...

00:14:40.757 --> 00:14:43.885
I'm the greatest! Whoo-hoo!

00:14:44.969 --> 00:14:47.222
Looks like we got the old Bender back.

00:14:47.305 --> 00:14:51.184
You know it, Porkpie.
Except for one thing...

00:15:01.110 --> 00:15:03.821
You know, as a major Hollywood director

00:15:03.905 --> 00:15:06.741
I'll be holding auditions
tonight for my next movie.

00:15:06.824 --> 00:15:09.827
And even though you're all young and naive

00:15:09.911 --> 00:15:12.497
I think you might just have what it takes.

00:15:16.125 --> 00:15:18.586
Hey, I'm trying to score here.

00:15:18.670 --> 00:15:21.172
Can't you read the "Do not disturb" sign?

00:15:26.010 --> 00:15:29.138
No! No!

00:15:34.435 --> 00:15:36.271
Greetings, Bender.

00:15:36.354 --> 00:15:39.107
Welcome to Robot Hell.

00:15:47.907 --> 00:15:49.951
What in hell happened
to Bender?

00:15:50.034 --> 00:15:52.328
Well, he didn't check out.
The ashtray's still here.

00:15:54.414 --> 00:15:57.500
Look, Nibbler's caught the scent
of vodka and motor oil.

00:15:57.917 --> 00:16:00.086
Go, Boy.
Follow that stench.

00:16:04.966 --> 00:16:06.801
I'm hallucinating this, right?

00:16:06.885 --> 00:16:08.720
No, Bender.

00:16:08.803 --> 00:16:11.055
Robot Hell is quite real.

00:16:11.139 --> 00:16:12.932
Here's our brochure.

00:16:14.184 --> 00:16:15.977
But I don't belong here.

00:16:16.060 --> 00:16:18.688
I don't like things
that are scary and painful.

00:16:18.980 --> 00:16:20.273
Sorry, Bender.

00:16:20.356 --> 00:16:23.318
You agreed to this when
you joined our religion.

00:16:23.401 --> 00:16:26.029
If you sin, you go to robot hell...

00:16:26.112 --> 00:16:28.406
For all eternity.

00:16:28.489 --> 00:16:30.783
Aw, hell... I mean heck.

00:16:30.867 --> 00:16:32.702
It's all right.
You can say that here.

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:38.875
Wait, I remember this place.

00:16:38.958 --> 00:16:40.543
They shut it down after all those people

00:16:40.627 --> 00:16:42.712
caught Salmonella from the flume ride.

00:16:48.593 --> 00:16:50.303
Hmm.

00:16:51.554 --> 00:16:52.555
Look.

00:16:52.639 --> 00:16:54.641
It's the symbol of Bender's old religion.

00:16:58.645 --> 00:17:00.271
Unbelievable.

00:17:00.438 --> 00:17:03.358
It's an actual,
factual Robot Hell.

00:17:03.566 --> 00:17:05.944
Who would have thought
hell would really exist?

00:17:06.027 --> 00:17:07.612
And that it would be in New Jersey?

00:17:07.695 --> 00:17:08.947
Actually...

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:14.619
We know all your sins, Bender,

00:17:14.702 --> 00:17:16.579
and for each one, we've prepared

00:17:16.663 --> 00:17:21.334
an agonizing and ironic
punishment. Gentlemen?

00:17:24.295 --> 00:17:26.089
Aw, crap... Singing.

00:17:26.172 --> 00:17:27.298
Mind if I smoke?

00:17:31.302 --> 00:17:33.638
Cigars are evil
You won't miss 'em

00:17:33.721 --> 00:17:36.307
We'll find ways
To simulate that smell

00:17:36.391 --> 00:17:37.934
What a sorry fella.

00:17:38.017 --> 00:17:40.103
Rolled up and smoked
Like a panatela

00:17:40.186 --> 00:17:43.690
Here on level one of robot hell

00:17:46.568 --> 00:17:48.778
Gambling's wrong
And so is cheating

00:17:48.862 --> 00:17:51.447
So is forging phony I.O.U.s

00:17:51.531 --> 00:17:53.491
Let's let Lady Luck decide

00:17:53.575 --> 00:17:55.577
What type of torture's justified

00:17:55.660 --> 00:17:58.079
I'm pit boss here
On level two

00:17:58.872 --> 00:18:00.874
Ooh, deep-fried robot.

00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:02.292
Just tell me why?

00:18:02.375 --> 00:18:04.460
Please read this 55-page warrant

00:18:04.544 --> 00:18:06.504
There must be robots worse than I

00:18:06.588 --> 00:18:08.590
We checked around,
There really aren't

00:18:08.673 --> 00:18:10.383
Then please let me explain

00:18:10.466 --> 00:18:12.468
My crimes were merely boyish pranks

00:18:12.552 --> 00:18:14.429
You stole from boy scouts, nuns and banks

00:18:14.512 --> 00:18:17.056
Aw, don't blame me, blame my upbringing

00:18:17.140 --> 00:18:19.475
Please stop sinning while I'm singing.

00:18:21.394 --> 00:18:23.646
Selling bootleg tapes is wrong

00:18:23.730 --> 00:18:26.149
Musicians need that income to survive

00:18:26.232 --> 00:18:27.817
Hey, Bender, going to make some noise

00:18:27.901 --> 00:18:30.236
With the hard drive scratched
By the Beastie Boys

00:18:32.113 --> 00:18:35.575
That's whatcha, whatcha, whatcha get
On level five

00:18:35.658 --> 00:18:37.118
I don't feel well

00:18:37.202 --> 00:18:38.995
it's up to us to rescue him

00:18:39.078 --> 00:18:41.456
Maybe he likes it here in hell

00:18:41.539 --> 00:18:43.416
It's us who tempted him to sin

00:18:43.499 --> 00:18:45.668
Maybe he's back at the motel

00:18:45.752 --> 00:18:47.545
Come on, Fry, don't be scared

00:18:47.629 --> 00:18:49.672
I'm sure at least
One of us will be spared

00:18:49.756 --> 00:18:51.758
So just sit back
Enjoy the ride

00:18:51.841 --> 00:18:54.010
My ass has blisters from the slide

00:18:56.304 --> 00:18:58.431
Fencing diamonds
Fixing cockfights

00:18:58.515 --> 00:19:00.808
Publishing indecent magazines

00:19:00.892 --> 00:19:02.602
You'll pay for every crime

00:19:02.685 --> 00:19:04.687
Knee-deep in electric slime

00:19:04.771 --> 00:19:07.065
You'll suffer till
The end of time

00:19:07.148 --> 00:19:09.526
Enduring tortures
Most of which rhyme

00:19:09.609 --> 00:19:13.863
Trapped forever here
in Robot Hell.

00:19:16.574 --> 00:19:19.035
Of course, that's just for starters.

00:19:23.498 --> 00:19:24.916
Bender, are you all right?

00:19:25.083 --> 00:19:27.460
No. Oh, they're tormenting me

00:19:27.544 --> 00:19:30.088
with up-tempo singing and dancing.

00:19:30.255 --> 00:19:32.215
All right, Beelzebot.

00:19:32.298 --> 00:19:34.092
What'll it going to take
to get our friend back?

00:19:34.175 --> 00:19:37.053
Sorry, but I hold all the cards here.

00:19:37.136 --> 00:19:38.179
There's nothing you can do.

00:19:38.263 --> 00:19:42.058
Now if you'll just sign
this fiddle contest waiver...

00:19:42.141 --> 00:19:44.269
Wait. What fiddle contest?

00:19:44.352 --> 00:19:48.982
Uh... The fairness in hell act of 2275

00:19:49.065 --> 00:19:51.943
requires me to inform you
that if you can best me

00:19:52.026 --> 00:19:56.364
in a fiddle contest,
you win back Bender's soul.

00:19:56.447 --> 00:19:58.116
As well as a solid gold fiddle.

00:19:58.241 --> 00:20:00.535
Wouldn't a solid gold fiddle
weigh hundreds of pounds

00:20:00.618 --> 00:20:01.786
and sound crummy?

00:20:01.870 --> 00:20:03.121
Well, it's mostly for show.

00:20:04.664 --> 00:20:06.124
Do you know how to play the fiddle?

00:20:06.207 --> 00:20:07.500
No, do you?

00:20:07.584 --> 00:20:09.294
No, but I used to play the drums.

00:20:09.377 --> 00:20:10.879
They're sort of similar.

00:20:10.962 --> 00:20:12.213
What happens if we lose?

00:20:12.338 --> 00:20:15.216
You'll only win a smaller silver fiddle.

00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:17.886
Also, I guess I'll kill one of you...

00:20:17.969 --> 00:20:18.970
Him.

00:20:19.053 --> 00:20:20.180
We'll do it.

00:20:20.263 --> 00:20:22.265
Very well, then.

00:20:22.348 --> 00:20:23.725
Beat this.

00:20:32.525 --> 00:20:33.902
Well, we're boned.

00:20:36.029 --> 00:20:37.238
Your turn.

00:20:43.244 --> 00:20:44.412
Ha!

00:20:44.495 --> 00:20:45.914
Time for the drum solo.

00:20:49.959 --> 00:20:50.960
Run!

00:20:59.844 --> 00:21:00.970
Whoa!

00:21:01.054 --> 00:21:02.347
Stop them!

00:21:02.430 --> 00:21:03.765
They cheated!

00:21:07.435 --> 00:21:08.978
Hallelujah

00:21:09.062 --> 00:21:10.647
Hallelujah

00:21:10.730 --> 00:21:12.315
Hallelujah, hallelujah...

00:21:16.903 --> 00:21:18.112
Hurry, Bender.

00:21:18.196 --> 00:21:21.908
I could if you dropped
the stupid gold violin.

00:21:21.991 --> 00:21:23.701
Oh, sorry.

00:21:30.875 --> 00:21:32.043
Don't worry, guys.

00:21:32.126 --> 00:21:35.171
I'll never be too good or too evil again.

00:21:35.255 --> 00:21:38.383
From now on, I'll just be me.

00:21:38.466 --> 00:21:42.387
Uh, do you think you could be
just a little less evil than that?

00:21:42.470 --> 00:21:43.596
I don't know.

00:21:43.680 --> 00:21:46.558
Do you think you could survive
a 700-foot fall?

00:21:46.641 --> 00:21:48.977
Good old bender.

00:21:53.773 --> 00:21:55.024
Oh, yeah, yeah.

00:21:55.108 --> 00:21:56.985
This one goes out to my man, Bender.

00:21:57.068 --> 00:21:59.362
Sending this one out, special dedication.

00:21:59.863 --> 00:22:00.864
To all my peoples in the robot home world.

00:22:02.615 --> 00:22:05.743
Yeah, yeah!
Big up with the Professor.

00:22:05.827 --> 00:22:09.372
My man, Dr. Zoidberg.
I'd like to shout out...

00:22:09.497 --> 00:22:11.541
A personal shout out to Leela.

00:22:11.624 --> 00:22:15.128
Fry! My man, Bender,

00:22:15.545 --> 00:22:17.964
Nibbler, Nibbler, in the house.

00:22:18.047 --> 00:22:20.717
Big shout out to all of Futurama!